{"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Defining Events"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow"],"anchor":"Guides","title":"Guides"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Derive an event’s conformances and schema from its declaration with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":", and constrain which values its properties may hold."}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/DefiningEvents","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros"},{"type":"text","text":") makes a struct an event from its declaration. It is a product of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its own that "},{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" leaves out, so only apps that use it build swift-syntax. It adds"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the "},{"code":"Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"BinaryCodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conformances, the event’s name, consent category and schema version"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when you give them, and a "},{"code":"schema","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", an "},{"code":"EventSchema","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" value that tooling reads:"}]},{"code":["import EventMacros","","@Event(name: \"checkout_started\", version: 2)","struct CheckoutStarted {","    var cartSize: Int","    var coupon: String?","}","","let tracker = Tracker()","tracker.track(CheckoutStarted(cartSize: 3, coupon: nil))","let properties = CheckoutStarted.schema.properties.map(\\.name)  \/\/ [\"cartSize\", \"coupon\"]"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The schema holds the name, the version, the consent category and each stored property’s name, its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"type as written, its optionality and whether it has a default value, in declaration order. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"encoding writes each of those properties under its name, as a hand-written conformance does","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"), and a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" property keeps its redaction. A record stored before","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a property with a default value (","type":"text"},{"code":"var currency: String = \"USD\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") was added reads it as its default.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"version:"},{"type":"text","text":" counts breaking changes only, and is 1 when left out; "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChangingEvents","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" shows each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"kind of change. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"consent:"},{"type":"text","text":" sets the event’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"consentCategory"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event(consent: .advertising)"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A stored property whose type isn’t ","type":"text"},{"code":"BinaryCodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a compile error that names it:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"static method 'requireBinaryCodable(position:)' requires that 'Coordinate' conform to 'BinaryCodable'","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"So are ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on anything but a struct, and a stored property without a type annotation. Static","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and computed properties are left out. The struct keeps its memberwise initializer.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"anchor":"Constraining-properties","type":"heading","text":"Constraining properties"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A property’s type says what kind of value it holds; a constraint says which values of that kind","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are valid. A rule the type can enforce belongs in the type: a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Refined","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value satisfies every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"constraint of its ","type":"text"},{"code":"Refinement","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from the moment it is made. Rules a plain ","type":"text"},{"code":"String","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" can’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"carry are declared beside the property with ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Constrained","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"), and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tracker checks them:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["enum CouponCode: Refinement {","    static let constraints: [Constraint<String>] = [.pattern(\"^[A-Z0-9]{6}$\", example: \"SPRING\")]","}","","@Event(name: \"search_performed\")","struct SearchPerformed {","    @Constrained(.minLength(1), .maxLength(200))","    var query: String","    @Constrained(.minimum(0))","    var resultCount: Int","    var coupon: Refined<String, CouponCode>?","}","","let coupon = try? Refined<String, CouponCode>(checked: \"spring\")  \/\/ nil: UnsatisfiedConstraint.pattern","let tracker = Tracker()","tracker.track(SearchPerformed(query: \"\", resultCount: 3, coupon: Refined(\"SPRING\")))","await tracker.finish()","for await report in tracker.rejectionReports {","    print(report)  \/\/ search_performed: \"query\" breaks minLength 1 (1 rejected)","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The keywords are JSON Schema’s: "},{"code":"minLength","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"maxLength","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (in Unicode scalars) and "},{"code":"pattern","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a string, "},{"code":"minimum","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"maximum","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for a number, "},{"code":"minItems","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"maxItems","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for an array. Each is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"offered only for the types it applies to, with its bound in the property’s own type, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":".minLength","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on an "},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"code":".minimum(0.5)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on an "},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", is a compile error. In "},{"code":"@Constrained","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so is a lower bound above its upper bound, a pattern that doesn’t compile, and a pattern whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"example","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" it, or another keyword of the property, rejects. In a "},{"code":"Refinement","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", those trap when its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"constraints are built. "},{"code":"Refined","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s plain initializer traps on a value that breaks its rule, as an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Array","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" subscript does out of range; "},{"code":"init(checked:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" throws the "},{"code":"UnsatisfiedConstraint","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instead."}]},{"level":3,"anchor":"Rejected-events","type":"heading","text":"Rejected events"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tracker’s worker checks each event’s declared constraints before anything else, never on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"caller. An event that breaks one is rejected: never enriched, held by a consent, written to a store"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or delivered. Each rejection is reported on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tracker.rejectionReports"},{"type":"text","text":" as a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RejectionReport"},{"type":"text","text":" naming"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the event, the property and the keyword, and in debug builds it is logged at error level too."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Unread reports merge, one per event, property and keyword, counting the rejections and the range of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"times they were tracked, so a broken call site in a loop can’t fill memory."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record that a store recovered from an earlier run is checked again, and the store forgets one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that a constraint added since rejects. A stored "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Refined"},{"type":"text","text":" value whose rule no longer accepts it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"doesn’t decode, and the store reports it. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" property takes no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Constrained"},{"type":"text","text":" keywords,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"since checking one would reveal it; a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive<Refined<…>>"},{"type":"text","text":" enforces its rule as it is made."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both kinds of constraint are part of the event’s schema. The exported tracking plan lists them"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"beside each property’s type, and each example payload satisfies them, using a pattern’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"example"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow"},{"type":"text","text":"). An array’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Refined"},{"type":"text","text":" elements are checked as they are made, but their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rules aren’t exported."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent\/definingevents"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent"]]},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Vendor-neutral analytics for Swift: typed events, tracked by a tracker and delivered in batches to any number of destinations.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent","title":"Traffluent","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent","role":"collection"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/PersistingRecords":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so a record the app tracked survives the process ending.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","title":"Persisting Records","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords","role":"article"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/ConsentGating":{"kind":"article","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Deliver an event only once the user grants the purpose it is collected for."}],"title":"Consent Gating","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/consentgating","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/SamplingEvents":{"kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Sampling Events","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep a seeded fraction of the events a tracker tracks, event by event or a whole session at once."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/samplingevents","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/SessionsAndStandardContext":{"kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Sessions and Standard Context","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Stamp every event with its session and with the app, device, system, locale and network it was tracked on."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/sessionsandstandardcontext","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TrackingPlanWorkflow":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Export the JSON Schema of every event an app tracks, commit it, and fail the build when the events stop matching it."}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow","title":"Exporting and Checking a Tracking Plan","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingplanworkflow","role":"article"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/ChangingEvents":{"kind":"article","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An event’s version counts the changes that records stored before them can’t be read through, and only those. A compatible change keeps the version; a breaking one raises it."}],"title":"Changing an Event","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/changingevents","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChangingEvents"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/AutomaticTracking":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Track screen views, control activations and the app’s lifecycle without a call at each place they happen."}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking","title":"Automatic Tracking","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/automatictracking","role":"article"},"doc://EventMacros/documentation/EventMacros":{"type":"topic","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros","title":"EventMacros","url":"\/documentation\/eventmacros","role":"collection"}}}